# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every platform.
# On Windows, Git's default (core.autocrlf=true) would otherwise check shell scripts out with
# CRLF endings: docker/api-entrypoint.sh is copied into the api image, and with CRLF the
# container cannot start, so `docker compose up` would fail. LF everywhere also keeps Prisma's
# migration checksums identical on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
